---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, LINKEDIN_URL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="A little about me and why I write here." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About me</h1>
			<p>
				Hi, I'm Tushita. I'm a software developer based in Montreal with nearly a decade of
				experience building backend systems, with a particular love for search, data platforms and
				distributed systems. I've worked on everything from knowledge graphs and search features to
				streaming APIs and cloud infrastructure, and I care a lot about keeping complex things simple.
			</p>
			<p>
				My day-to-day toolbox includes Scala, Java and Python, along with technologies like
				Postgres, Elasticsearch, Kafka, Neo4j and AWS. Outside of work I enjoy being in nature,
				staying fit, making art, and building community. I love connecting with people.
			</p>

			<h2>Why this blog?</h2>
			<p>
				I build side projects to learn, and writing about them is the best way I know to make the
				lessons stick. But I also have opinions about how software gets built: engineering
				practices, team processes, code review, and the books and blog posts that shape how I think
				about all of it. This is where I put those down too.
			</p>
			<p>
				Every post lives in a series. You can browse them all on the <a href="/series">blog series</a> page.
			</p>

			<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
			<p>
				You can find my code on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> and connect with me on
				<a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a>. The views on this site are my own.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
